00:00:02,650 --> 00:00:09,090
Comparing numbers within 100.

2
00:00:12,650 --> 00:00:19,050
Example 1: Compare numbers 43 and 49.

3
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:26,660
Fill in the blank.

4
00:00:28,980 --> 00:00:39,760
Number 43 consists of 4 tens and 3 ones

5
00:00:41,500 --> 00:00:51,460
Number 49 consists of 4 tens and 9 ones

6
00:00:53,900 --> 00:01:08,920
Numbers 43 and 49 have the same tens digit equal to 4, so we compare the ones digit.

7
00:01:10,980 --> 00:01:19,600
We see 3 < 9, so 43 < 49

